<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Telefonica upped.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Telefonica upped.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings analyst Patrick Jurczak raised his rating on Telefonica del Peru SA Tuesday to buy from hold.</p>
<p>-- The company &quot;is expected to benefit from Peru's increased economic activity and see strong earnings growth in 1997 from its cellular and cable TV activities,&quot; he wrote in an analysis.</p>
<p>-- Jurczak and analyst Andrew Friedman set a new 12-month price target of $32, up from $24.  &quot;Combined with a 3.5 percent dividend yield, this target represents a potential 36.1 percent total return.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's American Depositary Receipts opened up 3/8 at 24-1/2.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
